1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,834
Welcome to the world of numbers!

2
00:00:02,924 --> 00:00:06,323
This is Ollie. Ollie is a one.

3
00:00:06,383 --> 00:00:09,467
Today we will learn about tens and ones.

4
00:00:09,497 --> 00:00:10,996
Let's go!

5
00:00:11,206 --> 00:00:14,050
These little blocks are called ones.

6
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:15,985
Let's count them.

7
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:17,499
One.

8
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:18,819
Two.

9
00:00:18,879 --> 00:00:20,273
Three.

10
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:21,822
Four.

11
00:00:21,942 --> 00:00:24,117
Four ones make four.

12
00:00:24,417 --> 00:00:26,731
Now, watch this!

13
00:00:26,821 --> 00:00:28,890
Here are ten ones.

14
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:30,385
One.

15
00:00:30,386 --> 00:00:31,627
Two.

16
00:00:31,628 --> 00:00:33,003
Three.

17
00:00:33,004 --> 00:00:34,475
Four.

18
00:00:34,476 --> 00:00:35,971
Five.

19
00:00:35,972 --> 00:00:37,547
Six.

20
00:00:37,548 --> 00:00:39,124
Seven.

21
00:00:39,125 --> 00:00:40,395
Eight.

22
00:00:40,396 --> 00:00:41,797
Nine.

23
00:00:41,798 --> 00:00:43,217
Ten.

24
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:45,711
Ten ones make one ten!

25
00:00:45,921 --> 00:00:48,380
Ten ones equals one ten.

26
00:00:48,531 --> 00:00:51,975
This is Tenny. Tenny is a ten.

27
00:00:52,185 --> 00:00:54,144
Let's build a number.

28
00:00:54,234 --> 00:00:56,333
Here are three tens.

29
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:58,672
And here are four ones.

30
00:00:58,762 --> 00:01:02,001
Three tens and four ones make thirty-four.

31
00:01:02,361 --> 00:01:06,125
In thirty-four, the three is in the tens place.

32
00:01:06,215 --> 00:01:08,824
And the four is in the ones place.

33
00:01:08,914 --> 00:01:11,033
Three tens is thirty.

34
00:01:11,123 --> 00:01:13,347
And four ones is four.

35
00:01:13,438 --> 00:01:16,436
Thirty plus four equals thirty-four.

36
00:01:16,736 --> 00:01:18,971
Let's try another number.

37
00:01:19,061 --> 00:01:21,235
Here are five tens.

38
00:01:21,325 --> 00:01:23,149
And two ones.

39
00:01:23,239 --> 00:01:25,388
That makes fifty-two.

40
00:01:25,688 --> 00:01:30,637
Which number is greater? Thirty-four, or fifty-two?

41
00:01:33,017 --> 00:01:35,251
Look at the tens first.

42
00:01:35,341 --> 00:01:38,270
Five tens is more than three tens.

43
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:41,630
So fifty-two is greater than thirty-four.

44
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:45,358
A two-digit number is made of tens and ones.

45
00:01:45,448 --> 00:01:48,687
Three tens and four ones make thirty-four.

46
00:01:48,837 --> 00:01:52,457
Great job! See you next time!
